(Stamp Taxes on Drafts, Checks and Promissory Notes[1]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([1] Based on Treasury Regulations No. 55.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Revenue Act of 1918 imposes a tax on drafts and checks, payable) Tj T*
(otherwise than at sight or on demand, upon their acceptance or) Tj T*
(delivery, whichever is prior, within the territorial jurisdiction of) Tj T*
(the United States, and on promissory notes, except those listed below) Tj T*
(as exempt, and on each renewal of the same. The term ?United States?) Tj T*
(includes the states, the District of Columbia, Hawaii and Alaska.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The tax is at the rate of 2 cents on each $100 or fractional part) Tj T*
(thereof. On amounts not in excess of $100 the tax is 2 cents.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Any instrument or writing operating as a renewal of a promissory note) Tj T*
(is taxable, but the mere suspension of payment or forbearance does not) Tj T*
(constitute a taxable renewal within the meaning of the law, nor does) Tj T*
ET
