(_Cancellation of Stamps_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Any person using or affixing stamps must so deface the same as to) Tj T*
(render them unfit for further use by writing or stamping his initials) Tj T*
(and the date thereon with ink, or by cutting and canceling such stamp) Tj T*
(with a machine or punch, which will affix the initials and date.) Tj T*
(The cancellation should not so deface the stamp as to prevent its) Tj T*
(denomination and genuineness from being readily determined.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In addition to the above, stamps of the value of 10 cents or more must) Tj T*
(have three parallel incisions made by some sharp instrument lengthwise) Tj T*
(through the stamp after the same has been attached to the document,) Tj T*
(except where the stamps are cancelled by perforation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Use of Cancelled Stamps--Refunds_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A stamp affixed to an instrument and cancelled cannot lawfully be) Tj T*
(removed and attached to another instrument. Refund will be made by) Tj T*
(the collector of internal revenue for amounts paid for stamps used in) Tj T*
(excess of requirements, or on instruments not actually effective and) Tj T*
(for which a substitute is prepared and stamped, or on instruments not) Tj T*
(subject to tax.) Tj T*
